{title: O for a Thousand Tongues to Sing}
{artist: Charles Wesley}
{key: G}
{tempo: 96}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune AZMON - Carl G. Gläser (1828), arr. Lowell Mason (1839)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1739, tune 1839: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
O [G]for a [D]thousand [G]tongues to [C]sing
My [G]great Re[D]deemer's [G]praise[D],
The [G]glories [D]of my [Em]God and [Bm]King,
The [C]tri[G]umphs [D]of His [G]grace!
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
My [G]gracious [D]Master [G]and my [C]God,
As[G]sist me [D]to pro[G]claim[D],
To [G]spread through [D]all the [Em]earth a[Bm]broad
The [C]hon[G]ors [D]of Thy [G]name.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Je[G]sus! the [D]name that [G]charms our [C]fears,
That [G]bids our [D]sorrows [G]cease[D];
'Tis [G]music [D]in the [Em]sinner's [Bm]ears,
'Tis [C]life, [G]and [D]health, and [G]peace.
{end_of_verse}
